     "titulo": "The future",
     "texto": [
      "Danish has no future tense. It uses the **present**, as English often does too:\n\n- Jeg **ringer** lige til ham. → I'll call him right now.\n- Jeg **kommer** torsdag. → I'm coming on Thursday.\n- Jeg **køber** nogle tabletter, når jeg er i byen. → I'll buy some pills when I'm in town."
